/bin/bash -lc "nl -ba .claude/rules/script-md-siblings.md | sed -n '1,220p'" in <OPERATOR_REPO_PATH>
 succeeded in 0ms:
     1	---
     2	paths: ["scripts/**/*.{sh,py}", "skills/**/scripts/**/*.{sh,py}", ".claude/skills/**/scripts/**/*.{sh,py}", "skills/shared/*.md"]
     3	---
     4	
     5	# Script Documentation Siblings
     6	
     7	Every `.sh` / `.py` script under `scripts/` and `skills/<name>/scripts/`
     8	has a sibling `<basename>.md` beside it (e.g.
     9	`scripts/redact-secrets.md` beside `scripts/redact-secrets.sh`) covering
    10	purpose, primary callers, invariants, Makefile wiring, harness, and
    11	edit-in-sync rules. Read it before editing a script; update it in the
    12	same PR as any behavior change. Two co-location patterns are permitted,
    13	neither is an exemption from the file-existence rule:
    14	
    15	- **Primary owns the full contract.** When a primary script has a
    16	  sourced-only library (`scripts/lib-*.sh` — no shebang) and/or a
    17	  regression harness (`scripts/test-*.sh` for the primary), the primary
    18	  `.md` owns the full contract and cites related paths. Library and
    19	  harness still get sibling `.md` stubs so every `.sh` stays
    20	  discoverable and auditable; stubs point to the primary `.md`.
    21	- **Cross-tree harnesses.** A harness may live under `scripts/test-*.sh`
    22	  while its primary lives at `skills/<name>/scripts/<primary>.sh` (e.g.
    23	  `scripts/test-post-scaffold-hints.sh` testing
    24	  `skills/create-skill/scripts/post-scaffold-hints.sh`). The primary
    25	  `.md` owns the full contract; the harness in `scripts/` still gets a
    26	  sibling `.md` stub naming its primary.
    27	
    28	**Caller surface for shared scripts.** When changing a script under
    29	`scripts/`, grep for callers across `skills/`, `hooks/`,
    30	`.claude/settings.json`, `.github/workflows/`, and other scripts before
    31	finalizing.
    32	
    33	For canonical documentation files (`skills/shared/*.md`), update triggers
    34	live at the file bottom.
    35	
    36	This rule's `paths:` intentionally covers nested
    37	`skills/**/scripts/**/*.{sh,py}` so future skill script layouts inherit
    38	the same sibling-contract invariant.

