./larch-logs/implement/BF0B9FA8-A0E9-464B-A133-5298ED9D193A/round-4/cursor-specialist-security-output-phase3.txt:11:1. **security** `scripts/check-reviewers.sh:155-156` — **Latent** — cursor authentication tokens that `cursor_auth_argv` injects into `CURSOR_AUTH_ARGS` appear in the process argv (`cursor agent … --api-key $TOKEN`) for the duration of the probe subprocess, making them visible in `/proc/$pid/cmdline` and `ps aux` output to co-users. This is a pre-existing pattern shared with all Cursor launchers and is not introduced by this diff; noting it here in case hardening (e.g., via environment variable passing instead of CLI args) is planned in a follow-up. Out of scope because this pattern predates the branch.
./larch-logs/implement/695D84DF-ED83-47FE-9429-B144D28368B3/execution-issues.ndjson:3:{"phase":"implement","step":"7a","category":"Out-of-Scope Observations","source":"execution-issues.md pre-bump","source_sha256":"077fa4e3592613d406098c8aeb3765af31773e4471b1b7b6eaad92e2098b2472","body":"\n1. **Nit** · `architecture` · **Branch scope vs launcher-only narrative** — The diff vs `main` includes large unrelated hunks (multiple committed [`larch-logs/implement/…`](larch-logs/implement/) trees, [`CHANGELOG.md`](CHANGELOG.md) entries, [`skills/design/scripts/tally-plan-review.sh`](skills/design/scripts/tally-plan-review.sh) / docs, Makefile shard churn, token/timing instrumentation, etc.). **Why out of scope:** the supplied **implementation_plan** excerpt does not enumerate those as launcher deliverables; they complicate plan-to-diff traceability for this review pass only.\n\n---\n\n**TSV (intended sidecar; not written to disk — read-only)**\n\n```text\nschema_version\tscope\tseverity\tfocus_area\tlocation\twhat\tscenario_or_breakage\tsuggested_fix\n1\tin_scope\tlatent\tcorrectness\tskills/implement/SKILL.md:Step2.3-QA-redispatch\tStep 2 Q/A redispatch documents three flags on run-step2-dispatch.sh while acceptance criterion (1) says top-3 SKILL blocks <=2 flags each\tBranch scored against literal acceptance text fails even though implementation_plan allows --answers exception\tAmend acceptance criteria to match planned --answers exception or redesign answers handoff to stay within two flags\n1\tin_scope\tnit\tarchitecture\tscripts/run-step5-review.md:Derived-sources\trun-id contract cites session-id only while run-step5-review.sh resolves RUN_ID from session-env parent-issue manifest then session-id\tIntegrators misconfigure or mis-debug RUN_ID precedence\tUpdate contract md to match resolve_run_id ordering\n1\tin_scope\tnit\tarchitecture\timplementation_plan:Step0-LARCH_AUTO_MODE\tPlan text demanded atomic append after write-session-env; implementation used write-session-env --auto-mode instead\tAudit trail expecting the exact append mechanism described in the plan sees a different mechanism\tNote superseding approach in plan or retro-edit plan doc for traceability\n1\tin_scope\tlatent\trisk-integration\tskills/implement/SKILL.md:Step5-main-agent-vote-required\tProse still embeds direct review-and-fix.sh argv for main-agent-vote-required path\tOrchestrator may reconstruct that invocation from markdown instead of a pinned launcher\tAdd narrow launcher or document as explicit low-arity exception\n1\tout_of_scope\tnit\tarchitecture\tdiff-vs-main breadth\tDiff contains many non-launcher files (larch-logs trees CHANGELOG tally-plan-review Makefile shards token marks)\tPlan fidelity reader cannot attribute all churn to the launcher plan\tNone required for launcher plan; split PRs for future work\n```\n  ```\n"}
./larch-logs/implement/1000C0E5-7A1A-4FDA-B63F-F6AD21030590/round-3/findings.md:58:- **Concern**: [important] Structured NS-retry success publishes the structured sidecar with cp instead of the planned mv. After success, STRUCTURED_SIDECAR may point at ORIG_OUTPUT.* while an identical file remains on the NS-retry path; plan assumed relocation off the retry path. Use mv as in the plan, or amend the plan/spec to require duplicate sidecars on disk.
./larch-logs/implement/086677CB-5DA8-4D45-9343-0C3506B2CE41/execution-issues.ndjson:1:{"phase":"implement","step":"7a","category":"External Reviewer Issues","source":"execution-issues.md pre-bump","source_sha256":"6ebd49fd401f4e11adf3ec5b0e5591e4387446396c521d2b566cfd127bc349b2","body":"\n- **Step review Step 3a — collect-agent-results.sh cursor NOT_SUBSTANTIVE failed (exit 0)**:\n  ```\nCOLLECTOR_STATUS=NOT_SUBSTANTIVE\nREVIEWER_FILE=<TMPDIR>/round-1/cursor-specialist-correctness-output.txt\nTOOL=cursor\nEXIT_CODE=0\n\n--- reviewer output ---\nGathering the branch diff and commit list for a read-only correctness review. We won't write the TSV sidecar file (read-only constraint); we'll include TSV lines you can save manually.\n\nVerifying stale CI copy (`of 10`), docs parallelism (`-j10`), and whether splitting citation harnesses breaks assumptions. Reading the affected files for exact lines.\n\nChecking for other references to \"10\" shards in CI/docs and whether `larch-logs` commits are typical for this repo.\n\nCalling CreatePlan to satisfy plan-mode while delivering the full review in the required format.\n\n\n\n\n--- diagnostic sidecar ---\n\n  ```\n\n- **Step review Step 3a — collect-agent-results.sh cursor NOT_SUBSTANTIVE failed (exit 0)**:\n  ```\nCOLLECTOR_STATUS=NOT_SUBSTANTIVE\nREVIEWER_FILE=<TMPDIR>/round-1/cursor-specialist-edge-cases-output.txt\nTOOL=cursor\nEXIT_CODE=0\n\n--- reviewer output ---\nGathering the branch diff and commit history for a read-only review. Reading the precomputed diff and running a non-mutating `git log`.\n\nVerifying the CI step label and whether committed `larch-logs` artifacts are intentional.\n\nConfirming duplicate check passed. CI step name still says \"of 10\". Creating the review summary plan.\n\n\n\n\n--- diagnostic sidecar ---\n\n  ```\n\n- **Step review Step 3a tsv-fallback — collect-findings.sh inline-TSV recovery cursor-specialist-structure-output.txt warning (exit 0)**:\n  ```\nGathering the diff, commit history, and full-file context for a read-only review. We won't write files (conflicts with hard read-only constraint); we'll include TSV records in the response.\n\nVerifying CI step text, docs for stale shard counts, and whether `test-validate-citations*` are still assigned. Checking Makefile shard lines for issues.\n\nHere is the structured review. **Read-only constraint:** I did not create or write any sidecar file on disk; the TSV block below is copy-pasteable if you need `diff.txt.tsv`.\n\n\n- **Step review Step 3a tsv-fallback — collect-findings.sh inline-TSV recovery cursor-specialist-testing-output.txt warning (exit 0)**:\n  ```\nGathering the diff and commit history for a read-only review. We won't create the TSV sidecar file (hard constraint: no file writes); we'll include TSV lines in the response for manual capture.\n\nVerifying shard assignments for duplicates/orphans and checking whether committed `larch-logs` files are intentional.\n\nReview is based on the cached diff, full [`Makefile`](Makefile) shard lines (line 50 is one physical line), [`.github/workflows/ci.yaml`](.github/workflows/ci.yaml) lines 162–187, [`docs/linting.md`](docs/linting.md), and a duplicate check (`awk` + `uniq -d` returned no duplicates). Per your read-only rule, **no files were written** (including the `.tsv` sidecar); the TSV block at the end is copy-pasteable to the path you would have used.\n\n**Commits** (`git merge-base HEAD main..HEAD`): `8b2b3ca Rebalance CI test-harness shards from 10 to 11 (closes #2252)`, `7d3172e chore(larch-logs): flush implement run 086677CB-5DA8-4D45-9343-0C3506B2CE41`.\n\n**Plan / CI alignment (positive)**: Matrix includes shard `11`; `test-harnesses` umbrella and `.PHONY` include `test-harnesses-11`; `test-harnesses-11` leads with `test-harness-shards-coverage` as required ([`Makefile`](Makefile) lines 49–50). [`docs/linting.md`](docs/linting.md) branch-protection list adds `test-harnesses (11)`. No duplicate harness names across `test-harnesses-*:` lines (checked).\n\n\n- **Step review Step 3a tsv-fallback — collect-findings.sh inline-TSV recovery cursor-specialist-security-output.txt warning (exit 0)**:\n  ```\nGathering the branch diff and commit history for a read-only security-focused review. We won't write the TSV sidecar (read-only constraint); we'll include structured TSV rows in the response if needed.\n\nVerifying the CI workflow step label line number and whether `larch-logs` is typically ignored.\n\n\n- **Step review Step 3a tsv-fallback — collect-findings.sh inline-TSV recovery cursor-specialist-plan-fidelity-output.txt warning (exit 0)**:\n  ```\nGathering the pre-computed diff and commit history for a read-only plan-fidelity review. `git log` and `git merge-base` are read-only.\n\nFetching exact line numbers for the CI step name and checking whether `docs/linting.md` still mentions `-j10`.\n\n## Plan fidelity review (branch vs `main`)\n\n**Commits** (`git merge-base HEAD main`..HEAD):\n\n- `8b2b3ca` Rebalance CI test-harness shards from 10 to 11 (closes #2252)\n- `7d3172e` chore(larch-logs): flush implement run 086677CB-5DA8-4D45-9343-0C3506B2CE41\n\n**Plan traceability (Makefile / CI / docs):** The rebalance commit matches the stated plan: `test-harnesses-11` on `.PHONY` and the umbrella; comment block references `#2252` and LPT; shards 1–11 match the planned prerequisite lists (including `test-harness-shards-coverage` first on shard 11); [`.github/workflows/ci.yaml`](.github/workflows/ci.yaml) matrix includes shard `11`; [`docs/linting.md`](docs/linting.md) updates “ten”→“eleven”, branch-protection bullet for `test-harnesses (11)`, and the “Changing the shard count” section to `11`.\n\n**Read-only constraint:** Per your instruction, no files were written (including the `.tsv` sidecar). The TSV block below is inline for copy/paste if you still want a sidecar file locally.\n\n---\n\n"}
./larch-logs/implement/086677CB-5DA8-4D45-9343-0C3506B2CE41/execution-issues.ndjson:9:{"phase":"implement","step":"7a","category":"In-Scope Findings","source":"execution-issues.md pre-bump","source_sha256":"1dd854b6f4d4bd2291a55da555b453fa025b7a8c83d16bdce07f00dd19919d38","body":"\n1. **`risk-integration` — Important** — [`.github/workflows/ci.yaml`](.github/workflows/ci.yaml):186 — The step name is still `Run test harnesses (shard ${{ matrix.shard }} of 10)` while the matrix now includes shard `11`. In the Actions UI and logs, shard 11 jobs are labeled “of 10,” which is wrong and can confuse triage when comparing matrix cells to docs. **Suggested fix:** Change the suffix to `of 11` (or remove the hard-coded total if you prefer a neutral label).\n\n2. **`code-quality` — Important** (plan / requirements) — [`docs/linting.md`](docs/linting.md):22 — The **Usage → CI** bullet still says the matrix runs `make test-harnesses-1` through `make test-harnesses-10`, but the branch updates other prose to eleven shards and [`ci.yaml`](.github/workflows/ci.yaml) runs eleven cells. **Concrete scenario:** Someone reads only the top of `linting.md` and believes CI still stops at shard 10. **Suggested fix:** Update that phrase to `test-harnesses-11`.\n\n3. **`code-quality` — Important** — [`scripts/test-harness-shards-coverage.md`](scripts/test-harness-shards-coverage.md):26-27 — The script’s sibling contract still says the last partition-guard shard is `test-harnesses-10:` and that the umbrella spans `test-harnesses-1` through `test-harnesses-10`. After this change, the Makefile’s last shard is `test-harnesses-11`. **Scenario:** Contributors following the script’s `.md` neighbor doc get the wrong mental model for “last shard” and umbrella span. **Suggested fix:** Point at `test-harnesses-11` or describe “highest `N` discovered from the Makefile” without a stale literal.\n\n4. **`code-quality` — Nit** — [`docs/linting.md`](docs/linting.md):42 — Parallel-local guidance still says `make -j10 test-harnesses` even though eleven shard targets exist. **Suggested fix:** Use `-j11` or wording like “up to the shard count.”\n\n5. **`code-quality` — Nit** — [`larch-logs/implement/086677CB-5DA8-4D45-9343-0C3506B2CE41/manifest.json`](larch-logs/implement/086677CB-5DA8-4D45-9343-0C3506B2CE41/manifest.json):10 — The committed manifest has `\"status\": \"in-progress\"` and `\"pr_number\": null`, unlike the “committed alongside the PR” completed-run shape described in [`docs/run-logs.md`](docs/run-logs.md). **Scenario:** Anyone treating `larch-logs/` as a finished-run archive gets a mid-flight snapshot. **Suggested fix:** Either complete the run and flush a terminal manifest or omit this directory from the change set if it was accidental.\n\n**Plan verification (structure):** [`Makefile`](Makefile) adds `test-harnesses-11`, extends the umbrella and `.PHONY`, moves `test-harness-shards-coverage` to the first prerequisite of the new last shard, and rebalance comments reference #2252 as planned. [`docs/linting.md`](docs/linting.md) branch-protection and “Changing the shard count” sections were updated per plan, but the early **Usage** paragraph was not (finding 2). A duplicate-harness scan across all `test-harnesses-*:` prerequisite tokens returned no duplicates (read-only `awk` + `sort | uniq -d`).\n\n---\n\n"}
