./larch-logs/implement/91719292-65E2-4439-A960-CC1AE225F7D0/execution-issues.ndjson:4:{"phase":"implement","step":"7a","category":"Structured TSV (read-only: sidecar file not written)","source":"execution-issues.md pre-bump","source_sha256":"b1bbaf8723cc5f354385be35329d94ec0f4ac23e3b53dc202a246fba4f30b49f","body":"\nPer your HARD CONSTRAINTS, no `.tsv` file was created on disk. Below is the sidecar content you can save manually if needed.\n\n```text\nschema_version\tscope\tseverity\tfocus_area\tlocation\twhat\tscenario_or_breakage\tsuggested_fix\n1\tin_scope\timportant\tarchitecture\tlarch-logs/implement/91719292-65E2-4439-A960-CC1AE225F7D0/manifest.json; larch-logs/implement/91719292-65E2-4439-A960-CC1AE225F7D0/plan-goals-test.md; larch-logs/implement/91719292-65E2-4439-A960-CC1AE225F7D0/plan-review-tally.json\tBranch adds implement run artifacts despite plan stating two documentation edits and no other changes.\tPR scope and history include unrelated in-progress implement run state; contradicts explicit plan scope.\tRemove the larch-logs/implement/91719292-... commit or files; keep only the two planned documentation edits.\n1\tin_scope\tnit\tcorrectness\tscripts/larch-log-batches.md:31-69\tNew section follows full Tally subsection rather than immediately after the H2 only.\tNone for readers; minor deviation from literal plan phrasing.\tOptional: move section if strict heading-adjacency is required.\n```\n  ```\n"}
./larch-logs/implement/91719292-65E2-4439-A960-CC1AE225F7D0/execution-issues.ndjson:13:{"phase":"implement","step":"7a","category":"Structured TSV (not written to disk)","source":"execution-issues.md pre-bump","source_sha256":"0fc05c690046895e49aefe285c4d34ba16327bedd2060aa04d044ba1ba12bfc3","body":"\n```text\nschema_version\tscope\tseverity\tfocus_area\tlocation\twhat\tscenario_or_breakage\tsuggested_fix\n1\tin_scope\timportant\tcorrectness\tlarch-logs/implement/91719292-65E2-4439-A960-CC1AE225F7D0/manifest.json:1-20\tCommitted implement run artifacts and in-progress manifest are outside the stated doc-only scope.\tPR described as two doc edits merges unrelated RUN_ID tree; manifest shows status in-progress and pr_number null, misleading run-log consumers.\tRemove larch-logs commit or exclude that directory from this branch.\n1\tin_scope\tlatent\tcorrectness\tskills/implement/SKILL.md:370;scripts/larch-log-batches.md:50-55\tDocs say json-lines sanitizer requires jq -c; sanitizer only validates per-line JSON.\tOrchestrators may think non-jq compact one-liners are invalid.\tAlign wording with line-wise JSON validation; present jq -nc as the recommended pattern.\n1\tin_scope\tnit\tcorrectness\tscripts/larch-log-batches.md:54-55;skills/implement/SKILL.md:370\tAbsolute statement that jq -n without -c always yields multi-line output.\tRare jq outputs could be single-line; doc is slightly over-broad.\tSoften wording to typical behavior.\n1\tin_scope\tnit\tcode-quality\tskills/implement/SKILL.md:370\tSection sign in cross-reference.\tMinor style mismatch with repo guidance.\tUse plain language or a markdown link instead of .\n```\n\n**Plan / requirements verification (summary):**  \n- `scripts/larch-log-batches.md`: New `## oos-issues record schema` after tally section; single-line requirement; `jq -n` vs `-nc` warning; schema fields; `jq -nc` example; sanitization — **present and aligned** with plan.  \n- `skills/implement/SKILL.md` Carve-outs: **`jq -nc` mandate, warning, schema, `--arg body`, pointer to batches doc** — **present and aligned** with plan.  \n- **Completeness gap vs plan/feature:** extra `larch-logs/implement/...` files are **not** in the plan or feature description.  \n- **No contradiction** between feature description and plan on the two doc edits; the **code branch** adds unplanned artifacts.\n\n**Read-only note:** `git log $(git merge-base HEAD main)..HEAD --oneline` was run (read-only). The precomputed diff was read from the given cache path. No files were written or modified.\n  ```\n"}
