read-only constraint; structured rows are in the fenced block at the end so you can save them as a sidecar locally if needed.\n\n\n- **Step review Step 3a tsv-fallback — collect-findings.sh inline-TSV recovery cursor-specialist-plan-fidelity-output.txt warning (exit 0)**:\n  ```\nGathering the diff and commit history for a plan-fidelity review (read-only).\n\nSearching the diff for planned artifacts and reading key sections.\n\nChecking how Step 11 refresh interacts with the metadata comment content.\n\nHere is the plan-fidelity review. Read-only mode prevents writing a `.tsv` sidecar on disk; the same TSV rows appear in a fenced block at the end.\n\n---\n\n\n- **Step review Step 3a tsv-fallback — collect-findings.sh inline-TSV recovery cursor-specialist-structure-output.txt warning (exit 0)**:\n  ```\nGathering the branch diff and commit list for a read-only review. We can't write the TSV sidecar file due to your hard constraint against file mutations; we'll include the TSV records in the response in a delimited block you can save if needed.\n\nReading the large diff in sections and searching for key files.\n\nReading SKILL.md diff continuation and core new scripts from the diff file.\n\nVerifying the `awk` line in `refresh-execution-issues.sh` and whether `write-final-report` is duplicated in the repo.\n\nCommits on branch vs `main` (from your command):\n\n- `72c59150` — Address code review feedback (round 1)  \n- `49c4f2d3` — chore(larch-logs): flush implement run 7D5FECB5-6CB7-42F5-B98F-50D8759849EE  \n- `661d1db6` — Factor /implement prompt-side steps into scripts  \n\n**Read-only constraint:** I did not write any files. The instructions asked for a TSV sidecar on disk; that would mutate the filesystem, so the TSV records appear only in the fenced block at the end (you can save them as `diff.txt.tsv` locally if needed).\n\n\n- **Step review Step 3a tsv-fallback — collect-findings.sh inline-TSV recovery cursor-specialist-testing-output.txt warning (exit 0)**:\n  ```\nGathering the branch diff and commit history for a read-only review focused on tests, CI, and regression risk.\n\nSearching the diff for test harnesses, Makefile wiring, and script additions.\n\nReviewed the precomputed diff (including `Makefile`, `agent-lint.toml`, `skills/implement/SKILL.md`, new `skills/implement/scripts/*`, test harnesses, and committed `larch-logs/implement/7D5FECB5-6CB7-42F5-B98F-50D8759849EE/*`). Commits on branch vs `main`: `661d1db6 Factor /implement prompt-side steps into scripts`, `49c4f2d3 chore(larch-logs): flush implement run …`, `72c59150 Address code review feedback (round 1)`.\n\nRead-only constraint: no sidecar file was written on disk. Below is the same TSV in a fenced block you can save manually if needed.\n\n\n- **Step review Step 3a tsv-fallback — collect-findings.sh inline-TSV recovery cursor-specialist-edge-cases-output.txt warning (exit 0)**:\n  ```\nGathering the pre-computed diff and commit history (read-only git commands), then reviewing for edge cases and failure recovery.\n\nScanning the large diff for changed files and reading critical sections.\n\nReading new scripts and key SKILL.md hunks for edge-case analysis. We can't write the TSV sidecar under read-only constraints; we'll include TSV records in the response.\n\nNoting `implement-finalize.sh` still invokes `cleanup-tmpdir.sh` directly. Checking `launch-claude-subprocess.sh` for `--allow-root` semantics:\n\n\n- **Step review Step 3a tsv-fallback — collect-findings.sh inline-TSV recovery cursor-specialist-plan-fidelity-output.txt warning (exit 0)**:\n  ```\nGathering the diff and commit history for a plan-fidelity review (read-only).\n\nSearching the diff for plan-relevant paths and reading key sections.\n\nRead-only review is complete. The diff introduces the nine scripts plus tests, Makefile shard wiring, `agent-lint.toml` excludes, and `SKILL.md` orchestration updates. Below is plan-fidelity output in your requested shape.\n\n**Read-only note:** I cannot write the `.tsv` sidecar to disk in this mode. The TSV block at the end is the exact sidecar payload to save manually (for example next to your review artifact).\n\n---\n\n"}
