ch-panel after waterfall.\tWaterfall reports DISPATCH_OK=false but review continues as if dispatch fully succeeded.\tParse DISPATCH_OK from dispatch_out and fail the round or define tested ignore semantics.\n1\tin_scope\tnit\tcode-quality\tskills/review/scripts/dispatch-panel.sh:128-133 scripts/dispatch-code-voters.sh:113-118 scripts/dispatch-plan-voters.sh:89-92\tUnquoted word-split when rebuilding output/tool arrays from KV strings.\tOutput paths with spaces would split incorrectly.\tAvoid set -- $var on paths; use safer splitting.\n1\tin_scope\tnit\tcode-quality\tlarch-logs/implement/443D5F3B-8C58-4765-B325-16924E02A34F/\tCommitted implement run artifacts add noise and stale HEALTHY strings under larch-logs.\tRepo-wide greps and clone size suffer for little consumer value.\tRemove run flush from PR or follow committed run-log hygiene.\n1\tout_of_scope\tnit\tcode-quality\tskills/review/scripts/test-review-core.md:10\tDoc still references both-down PANEL_MODE.\tReaders get outdated mental model of dispatch.\tUpdate doc in a separate doc-only pass.\n1\tout_of_scope\tnit\tcode-quality\tCHANGELOG.md\tHistorical entries mention removed health flags.\tNone for runtime; minor grep noise.\tLeave as history or add a new changelog entry for the feature separately.\n```\n  ```\n"}
./larch-logs/implement/443D5F3B-8C58-4765-B325-16924E02A34F/execution-issues.ndjson:49:{"phase":"implement","step":"7a","category":"Out-of-Scope Observations","source":"execution-issues.md pre-bump","source_sha256":"a8ba8cd836ba6e6726558619f3317679fa11097b1aeddb21a3b09bc20a6c8c30","body":"\n1. **Nit**, **risk-integration**, [`larch-logs/implement/443D5F3B-8C58-4765-B325-16924E02A34F/plan-goals-test.md`](larch-logs/implement/443D5F3B-8C58-4765-B325-16924E02A34F/plan-goals-test.md) (and similar) — Committed run logs still contain literal `CODEX_HEALTHY` / `CURSOR_HEALTHY` in pasted plan text. Out of scope for runtime behavior; only relevant if any automated acceptance grep scans the whole repo without excluding `larch-logs/`.\n\n---\n\n**Structured TSV (would be sidecar content; not written to disk per read-only constraint)**\n\n```text\nschema_version\tscope\tseverity\tfocus_area\tlocation\twhat\tscenario_or_breakage\tsuggested_fix\n1\tin_scope\timportant\tcorrectness\tscripts/dispatch-with-waterfall.sh:174-201\tcollect_phase matches summary blocks by exact REVIEWER_FILE=phase output path\tAfter collect-agent-results retry success REVIEWER_FILE points at *-retry.txt so awk finds no block status empty slot treated as failure spurious phase 2 3 and wrong outputs\tAlign summary rows to argv order or match original output plus retry suffix or add argv index to summary\n1\tin_scope\timportant\tcorrectness\tscripts/dispatch-with-waterfall.sh:256-262\tFALLBACK_COUNTER_FILE merge treats cat value with trailing newline as non numeric and resets prior to 0\tCounter file contains 3 newline merged count drops WARN threshold wrong\tFeed cat through tr -d newline or read -r with validation\n1\tin_scope\tlatent\trisk-integration\tskills/review/scripts/dispatch-panel.sh:193-198 scripts/dispatch-code-voters.sh:113-118 scripts/dispatch-plan-voters.sh:88-93\tUnquoted word split when parsing ALL_OUTPUT_FILES and ALL_OUTPUT_TOOLS from KV values\tPaths with spaces split across array indices wrong specialist or voter mapping\tUse NUL delimited transfer or indexed KVs or parse from manifest only\n1\tin_scope\tlatent\tarchitecture\tscripts/dispatch-with-waterfall.sh:194-198\tcap_hit grouped with OK skips further waterfall phases\tCap hit output may be incomplete versus a full external review\tTreat cap_hit as failure for promotion or document as terminal success explicitly\n1\tin_scope\tlatent\trisk-integration\tscripts/dispatch-code-voters.sh:69-155\tDISPATCH_OK reflects only waterfall not voter 1 rc\tVoter 1 fails while waterfall ok DISPATCH_OK true misleads automation\tCombine DISPATCH_OK with voter1_rc\n1\tin_scope\tnit\trisk-integration\tscripts/test-dispatch-with-waterfall.sh\tHarness omits several planned regression cases\tThreshold WARN and phase 3 hard fail paths lack coverage\tAdd tests from implementation plan\n1\tin_scope\tnit\tcode-quality\tskills/review/scripts/dispatch-panel.sh:97-131\tUnused launch_claude_slot helper after waterfall\tMaintainers may wire wrong path thinking Claude slot still used here\tRemove dead code or document why kept\n1\tout_of_scope\tnit\trisk-integration\tlarch-logs/implement/443D5F3B-8C58-4765-B325-16924E02A34F/plan-goals-test.md\tOld HEALTHY tokens in committed run log text\tNoise if repo wide grep includes larch-logs\tExclude larch-logs from grep or strip from committed logs\n```\n  ```\n"}
./larch-logs/implement/443D5F3B-8C58-4765-B325-16924E02A34F/execution-issues.ndjson:53:{"phase":"implement","step":"7a","category":"Out-of-Scope Observations","source":"execution-issues.md pre-bump","source_sha256":"1126a0a67738d589f64f5f19f6711d332d56598a60ce8f4be0f07a885e6de7d5","body":"\n1. **Nit** `risk-integration` — [`larch-logs/implement/443D5F3B-8C58-4765-B325-16924E02A34F/plan-goals-test.md`](larch-logs/implement/443D5F3B-8C58-4765-B325-16924E02A34F/plan-goals-test.md) (and similar committed run logs) still contain literal strings like `CODEX_HEALTHY` / `CURSOR_HEALTHY` inside pasted plan text. **Why out of scope:** not runtime code; also your stated acceptance grep targets `skills/`, `scripts/`, `docs/`, etc., where those tokens are already gone.\n\n---\n\n**Commits** (`git merge-base HEAD main`..HEAD): `9cdf84d5` Drop reviewer health state and add waterfall fallback; `b8e3b09e` chore(larch-logs): flush implement run …; `db4350ac` Fix shellcheck, markdownlint, and agent-lint issues in waterfall implementation.\n\n**Read-only note:** Hard constraints forbid writing a `.tsv` file on disk; structured rows are in the fenced block below (same schema you requested).\n\n```text\nschema_version\tscope\tseverity\tfocus_area\tlocation\twhat\tscenario_or_breakage\tsuggested_fix\n1\tin_scope\timportant\tcorrectness\tscripts/dispatch-with-waterfall.sh:174-201\tcollect_phase matches collector summary by exact REVIEWER_FILE=original path\tAfter collect-agent-results empty-output retry, STATUS=OK rows use REVIEWER_FILE=*-retry.txt while collect_phase searches for the pre-retry path; block stays empty so STATUS is treated as failure and waterfall escalates to the wrong tool or Claude despite a successful primary-tool retry.\tParse summary paragraphs by the same order as phase_outputs/collect argv, or add an explicit stable ORIG_OUTPUT key, or implement a vetted path-equivalence rule between retry and original outputs.\n1\tin_scope\tlatent\tcorrectness\tscripts/test-dispatch-with-waterfall.sh:1-88\tMissing planned regression cases for Phase-3 hard failure and WARN threshold\tThreshold / DISPATCH_OK / hard-fail regressions in dispatch-with-waterfall.sh would not fail CI.\tExtend test-dispatch-with-waterfall.sh per Phase 4e of the implementation plan (CLAUDE_STUB_FAIL + threshold cases).\n1\tin_scope\tnit\tcode-quality\tskills/review/scripts/dispatch-panel.sh:97-131\tUnused launch_claude_slot helper after waterfall refactor\tFuture edits may mistakenly “fix” or resurrect dead paths; references LAUNCH_CLAUDE without local definition.\tDelete the dead helper or document a single supported entrypoint.\n1\tout_of_scope\tnit\trisk-integration\tlarch-logs/implement/443D5F3B-8C58-4765-B325-16924E02A34F/plan-goals-test.md:1-40\tLegacy HEALTHY tokens only in committed run-log prose\tNoise for repo-wide greps outside the acceptance paths; not executed.\tNone required for runtime; optional log redaction if full-repo greps matter.\n```\n  ```\n"}
./larch-logs/implement/443D5F3B-8C58-4765-B325-16924E02A34F/code-review-tally.json:1:{"schema_version":1,"phase":"code-review","batch":"code-review-tally","mode":"simple","rounds":1,"accepted_count":16,"rejected_count":16,"body":"Rounds: 1 | Accepted: 16 | Rejected: 16\n\n# Review Round 1\n\n- Mode: `diff`\n- Accepted findings: 16\n- Rejected findings: 23\n\n## Accepted Findings\n\n### FINDING_1: **Important** `risk-integration` `scripts/dispatch-with-waterfall.sh:148` passes `--competition-notice \"$COMPETITION_NOTICE\"` to `launch-review.sh`, but `scripts/launch-review.sh:119` defines `--competition-notice` as a valueless flag. When `/review` has `competition-notice.md`, `skills/review/scripts/review-core.sh:189` forwards it, every external phase launch sees the notice path as an unknown flag, fails Phase 1 and Phase 2, and the whole panel falls through to Claude. Fix by forwarding only `--competition-notice` to `launch-review.sh` and add a waterfall test covering `--competition-notice`.\n- **Reviewer**: codex-generalist-output.txt\n- **Concern**: 1. **Important** `risk-integration` `scripts/dispatch-with-waterfall.sh:148` passes `--competition-notice \"$COMPETITION_NOTICE\"` to `launch-review.sh`, but `scripts/launch-review.sh:119` defines `--competition-notice` as a valueless flag. When `/review` has `competition-notice.md`, `skills/review/scripts/review-core.sh:189` forwards it, every external phase launch sees the notice path as an unknown flag, fails Phase 1 and Phase 2, and the whole panel falls through to Claude. Fix by forwarding only `--competition-notice` to `launch-review.sh` and add a waterfall test covering `--competition-notice`.\n- **Suggested revision**: Address the concern above.\n\n\n### FINDING_18: correctness: scripts/dispatch-with-waterfall.sh:61-68\n- **Reviewer**: cursor-specialist-edge-cases-output.txt\n- **Concern**: [important] No validation of NDJSON slot schema beyond jq parse Malformed slot rows yield silent Phase-3 Claude fallback or null paths Add post-parse validation and fail fast on invalid rows\n- **Suggested revision**: Address the concern above.\n\n\n### FINDING_2: **Important** `security` `skills/design/SKILL.md:647` evals raw KV output from `dispatch-with-waterfall.sh`, whose `ALL_OUTPUT_FILES` values are unquoted paths emitted by `scripts/dispatch-with-waterfall.sh:300-307`. A session path derived from `XDG_CACHE_HOME`/`HOME` with shell metacharacters, e.g. `XDG_CACHE_HOME='/tmp/larch;touch /tmp/pwn'`, can be reflected into `ALL_OUTPUT_FILES=...` and executed by the `eval`. Replace the eval with the line-by-line allowlist parser pattern already used in `skills/review/scripts/dispatch-panel.sh:117-126`.\n- **Reviewer**: codex-generalist-output.txt\n- **Concern**: 2. **Important** `security` `skills/design/SKILL.md:647` evals raw KV output from `dispatch-with-waterfall.sh`, whose `ALL_OUTPUT_FILES` values are unquoted paths emitted by `scripts/dispatch-with-waterfall.sh:300-307`. A session path derived from `XDG_CACHE_HOME`/`HOME` with shell metacharacters, e.g. `XDG_CACHE_HOME='/tmp/larch;touch /tmp/pwn'`, can be reflected into `ALL_OUTPUT_FILES=...` and executed by the `eval`. Replace the eval with the line-by-line allowlist parser pattern already used in `skills/review/scripts/dispatch-panel.sh:117-126`.\n- **Suggested revision**: Address the concern above.\n\n\n### FINDING_20: correctness: skills/research/SKILL.md:132-143\n- **Reviewer**: cursor-specialist-plan-fidelity-output.txt\n- **Concern**: [important] Step 0 incomplete migration from probe/health to presence Orchestrator is told to use fallback_probe_failed and sanitize *_PROBE_ERROR though new branches emit fallback_presence_failed and probes are no longer parsed Update the status enum text to include fallback_presence_failed and drop or retarget the *_PROBE_ERROR sanitization paragraph to keys that still exist\n- **Suggested revision**: Address the concern above.\n\n\n### FINDING_21: correctness: skills/review/scripts/dispatch-panel.sh:111-112 and scripts/dispatch-with-waterfall.sh:43-44,148-152\n- **Reviewer**: cursor-specialist-security-output.txt\n- **Concern**: [important] --competition-notice is wired with a file path into launch-review.sh which only accepts a boolean flag; the next token is treated as an unknown flag and external launches fail. Any run with --competition-notice-file set causes launch-review to exit 2 for affected slots; panel dispatch breaks instead of applying the notice. Pass only the boolean --competition-notice to launch-review.sh; inject file contents via prompt rendering or a dedicated --competition-notice-file contract on the launcher/renderer.\n- **Suggested revision**: Address the concern above.\n\n\n### FINDING_22: correctness: skills/shared/dialectic-protocol.md:144\n- **Reviewer**: cursor-specialist-testing-output.txt\n- **Concern**: [important] Scoping bullets corrupted (invalid SESSION_ENV_PATH concatenation; empty ``). Operators lose the no-session-env-mutation rule or misinterpret required collector behavior. Restore two explicit, syntactically valid bullets: forbid mutating session env; describe collect-agent-results invocation without placeholder corruption.\n- **Suggested revision**: Address the concern above.\n\n\n### FINDING_23: correctness: skills/shared/dialectic-protocol.md:248\n- **Reviewer**: cursor-specialist-testing-output.txt\n- **Concern**: [important] Wrong `${SESSION_ENV_PATH}session-env` interpolation in collector note. Misidentifies which file must not be updated during dialectic collection. Use the canonical session-env path variable/name consistent with session-setup/write-session-env.\n- **Suggested revision**: Address the concern above.\n\n\n### FINDING_25: risk-integration: docs/linting.md (test-dispatch-with-waterfall row)\n- **Reviewer**: cursor-specialist-testing-output.txt\n- **Concern**: [important] Doc claims stubbed launch-review/launch-claude-review; harness uses real scripts. False confidence about test isolation. Describe PATH-stubbed codex/cursor/claude with real launcher scripts.\n- **Suggested revision**: Address the concern above.\n\n\n### FINDING_26: risk-integration: docs/linting.md:182\n- **Reviewer**: cursor-specialist-testing-output.txt\n- **Concern**: [important] Doc claims PATH-stubbed launch-claude-subprocess and broader harness coverage than implemented. Maintainers skip needed tests for --agent-file and context forwarding. Update docs or extend test-launch-claude-review.sh to match claims.\n- **Suggested revision**: Address the concern above.\n\n\n### FINDING_28: risk-integration: scripts/dispatch-code-voters.md:1-48\n- **Reviewer**: cursor-specialist-edge-cases-output.txt\n- **Concern**: [important] Contract documents obsolete parallel launch wait-for-reviewers and wrong DISPATCH_OK meaning Mis-implemented fixes or wrong operational runbooks based on stale contract Rewrite dispatch-code-voters.md to match dispatch-code-voters.sh waterfall behavior\n- **Suggested revision**: Address the concern above.\n\n\n### FINDING_29: risk-integration: scripts/dispatch-plan-voters.md:5-16\n- **Reviewer**: cursor-specialist-edge-cases-output.txt\n- **Concern**: [important] Contract documents obsolete run-external-agent and wait path Same as above for plan-review voter ops Rewrite dispatch-plan-voters.md to match dispatch-plan-voters.sh\n- **Suggested revision**: Address the concern above.\n\n\n### FINDING_32: risk-integration: scripts/test-dispatch-code-voters.sh;scripts/test-dispatch-plan-voters.sh (post-change)\n- **Reviewer**: cursor-specialist-testing-output.txt\n- **Concern**: [important] Removed argv-shape and multi-case integration coverage from stub-plugin harnesses. Wrapper flag regressions in real launches slip past CI. Reintroduce focused invocation-log assertions or a smaller stub-plugin slice.\n- **Suggested revision**: Address the concern above.\n\n\n### FINDING_33: risk-integration: scripts/test-dispatch-with-waterfall.sh\n- **Reviewer**: cursor-specialist-testing-output.txt\n- **Concern**: [latent] No all-phase1-OK baseline case. Phase gating bugs when all externals succeed could go unnoticed. Add one success-only case with FALLBACK_COUNT=0 and expected tools.\n- **Suggested revision**: Address the concern above.\n\n\n### FINDING_35: risk-integration: skills/review/scripts/dispatch-panel.sh (vs main make_prompt)\n- **Reviewer**: cursor-specialist-security-output.txt\n- **Concern**: [important] COMPETITION_NOTICE_FILE is no longer concatenated into any prompt; only the static template from render-specialist-prompt --competition-notice applies. Operators lose custom competition instructions that previously reached at least the Claude scratch path on main. Re-add explicit safe inclusion of the file into prompts for each tool tier that must see it, or drop the CLI and document the behavior change.\n- **Suggested revision**: Address the concern above.\n\n\n### FINDING_37: risk-integration: skills/review/scripts/test-dispatch-panel.sh (post-change)\n- **Reviewer**: cursor-specialist-testing-output.txt\n- **Concern**: [important] Harness dropped hard panel, both-down, stdout cap, and sentinel assertions. 12-slot wiring or waterfall stdout regressions may reach main undetected. Add hard and both-absent cases; restore bounded stdout check if still required.\n- **Suggested revision**: Address the concern above.\n\n\n### FINDING_38: risk-integration: skills/shared/dialectic-protocol.md:139\n- **Reviewer**: cursor-specialist-testing-output.txt\n- **Concern**: [important] Prose says not present/responding while presence is PATH-static. Reintroduces deprecated health semantics for judge gating. Align wording with presence-only model; drop responding language.\n- **Suggested revision**: Address the concern above.\n\n\n\n\n## Rejected Code Review Findings\n\n### [rejected] FINDING_10\n\n### FINDING_10: architecture: skills/design/references/sketch-launch.md:7-8\n- **Reviewer**: cursor-specialist-plan-fidelity-output.txt\n- **Concern**: 