./larch-logs/implement/BA089E98-62A7-4BFF-9155-09A6109B82EB/round-1/findings.md:133:- **Concern**: [important] Missing CMD_JSON-only NOT_SUBSTANTIVE retry branch planned in Fix A steps 4-5 NOT_SUBSTANTIVE slots with only CMD_JSON meta never get the one-shot stronger-prompt relaunch; behavior diverges from plan. Implement run-external-agent.sh retry path for NOT_SUBSTANTIVE when OUTER_LAUNCHER absent but CMD_JSON valid, mirroring section 3.
./larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/code-review-tally.json:1:{"schema_version":1,"phase":"code-review","batch":"code-review-tally","mode":"simple","rounds":1,"accepted_count":68,"rejected_count":0,"body":"# Review Round 1\n\n- Mode: `diff`\n- Accepted findings: 68\n- Rejected findings: 0\n\n## Accepted Findings\n\n### FINDING_1: **BLOCKING**, `risk-integration`, `larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/manifest.json:1-20` plus sibling `plan-goals-test.md` and `plan-review-tally.json` (commit `c4a3b5d7`): The branch adds a committed implement run directory (manifest with `operator_cwd` / `operator_repo_root`, `status: in-progress`, issue `2187`, and plan artifacts). That is unrelated product noise for the sanitizer change, bloats the plugin repo, and ships another machine’s paths into every consumer checkout. **Concrete scenario:** Anyone cloning the repo gets this run snapshot in `larch-logs/` and the PR diff is dominated by operational data instead of the NDJSON guard. **Suggested fix:** Remove that directory from the branch (drop or rewrite the `chore(larch-logs): flush implement run …` commit) so only the intentional script/doc/test changes remain.\n- **Reviewer**: cursor-specialist-edge-cases-output.txt\n- **Concern**: 1. **BLOCKING**, `risk-integration`, `larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/manifest.json:1-20` plus sibling `plan-goals-test.md` and `plan-review-tally.json` (commit `c4a3b5d7`): The branch adds a committed implement run directory (manifest with `operator_cwd` / `operator_repo_root`, `status: in-progress`, issue `2187`, and plan artifacts). That is unrelated product noise for the sanitizer change, bloats the plugin repo, and ships another machine’s paths into every consumer checkout. **Concrete scenario:** Anyone cloning the repo gets this run snapshot in `larch-logs/` and the PR diff is dominated by operational data instead of the NDJSON guard. **Suggested fix:** Remove that directory from the branch (drop or rewrite the `chore(larch-logs): flush implement run …` commit) so only the intentional script/doc/test changes remain.\n- **Suggested revision**: Address the concern above.\n\n### FINDING_2: **Commits reviewed** (`git merge-base HEAD main..HEAD`): `9e392b54 Harden NDJSON batch sanitizers`, `c4a3b5d7 chore(larch-logs): flush implement run 018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4`.\n- **Reviewer**: \n- **Concern**: \n- **Suggested revision**: Address the concern above.\n\n### FINDING_3: **Important** (`risk-integration`) [larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/manifest.json](larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/manifest.json):1-20, [larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/plan-goals-test.md](larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/plan-goals-test.md):1-37, [larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/plan-review-tally.json](larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/plan-review-tally.json):1 (commit `c4a3b5d7 chore(larch-logs): flush implement run 018DCD66-...`): The branch diff includes committed `/implement` run artifacts under `larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-...`, which are **not** listed in the implementation plan’s “Files to modify” or in the feature description’s deliverables (those only name `scripts/larch-log-batches.sh`, `scripts/larch-log-batches.md`, `scripts/test-larch-log.sh`, `scripts/test-larch-log.md`, plus call-site audit). A reviewer bisecting `main..HEAD` therefore sees an unrelated second commit and extra tree churn beside the sanitizer/doc/test work, which obscures the intended functional change set and can create needless merge/rebase conflicts. **Suggested fix:** Remove that commit (or otherwise exclude these paths from the PR) so the branch contains only the planned `scripts/*` edits.\n- **Reviewer**: cursor-specialist-plan-fidelity-output.txt\n- **Concern**: 1. **Important** (`risk-integration`) [larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/manifest.json](larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/manifest.json):1-20, [larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/plan-goals-test.md](larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/plan-goals-test.md):1-37, [larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/plan-review-tally.json](larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/plan-review-tally.json):1 (commit `c4a3b5d7 chore(larch-logs): flush implement run 018DCD66-...`): The branch diff includes committed `/implement` run artifacts under `larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-...`, which are **not** listed in the implementation plan’s “Files to modify” or in the feature description’s deliverables (those only name `scripts/larch-log-batches.sh`, `scripts/larch-log-batches.md`, `scripts/test-larch-log.sh`, `scripts/test-larch-log.md`, plus call-site audit). A reviewer bisecting `main..HEAD` therefore sees an unrelated second commit and extra tree churn beside the sanitizer/doc/test work, which obscures the intended functional change set and can create needless merge/rebase conflicts. **Suggested fix:** Remove that commit (or otherwise exclude these paths from the PR) so the branch contains only the planned `scripts/*` edits.\n- **Suggested revision**: Address the concern above.\n\n### FINDING_4: **Important** `code-quality` (requirements: scope) — [`larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/manifest.json:1-20`](larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/manifest.json), [`plan-goals-test.md:1-37`](larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/plan-goals-test.md), [`plan-review-tally.json:1`](larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/plan-review-tally.json): The branch bundles a second commit that adds a fresh implement run snapshot (manifest still `in-progress`, local `operator_*` paths, and plan/tally copies) together with the sanitizer and test changes. That is unrelated surface area for a “harden NDJSON sanitizers” change, forces reviewers to treat run-log policy and PII-ish paths as part of the same merge, and is not called for in the feature description. **Suggested fix:** Drop these paths from the feature PR (or split a dedicated “flush run log” PR) so the merge stays limited to [`scripts/larch-log-batches.sh`](scripts/larch-log-batches.sh), [`scripts/larch-log-batches.md`](scripts/larch-log-batches.md), [`scripts/test-larch-log.sh`](scripts/test-larch-log.sh), and [`scripts/test-larch-log.md`](scripts/test-larch-log.md).\n- **Reviewer**: cursor-specialist-structure-output.txt\n- **Concern**: 1. **Important** `code-quality` (requirements: scope) — [`larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/manifest.json:1-20`](larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/manifest.json), [`plan-goals-test.md:1-37`](larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/plan-goals-test.md), [`plan-review-tally.json:1`](larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/plan-review-tally.json): The branch bundles a second commit that adds a fresh implement run snapshot (manifest still `in-progress`, local `operator_*` paths, and plan/tally copies) together with the sanitizer and test changes. That is unrelated surface area for a “harden NDJSON sanitizers” change, forces reviewers to treat run-log policy and PII-ish paths as part of the same merge, and is not called for in the feature description. **Suggested fix:** Drop these paths from the feature PR (or split a dedicated “flush run log” PR) so the merge stays limited to [`scripts/larch-log-batches.sh`](scripts/larch-log-batches.sh), [`scripts/larch-log-batches.md`](scripts/larch-log-batches.md), [`scripts/test-larch-log.sh`](scripts/test-larch-log.sh), and [`scripts/test-larch-log.md`](scripts/test-larch-log.md).\n- **Suggested revision**: Address the concern above.\n\n### FINDING_5: **Important** `risk-integration` `scripts/larch-log-batches.sh:12`, `scripts/larch-log-batches.sh:17`: the branch makes `review-findings` and `oos-issues` reject non-JSON append payloads, but the prompt call sites still do not define a concrete NDJSON record composer. `skills/review/SKILL.md:55` only tells the orchestrator to write `review-findings`, and `skills/implement/SKILL.md:44` / `skills/implement/SKILL.md:1740` still describe the OOS append flow without showing how to wrap the markdown blocks into one JSON line. Concrete failure path: a `/review` or `/implement` run reaches those append steps with the existing markdown findings/OOS artifact, `log-phase.sh` or `larch-log.sh append` passes it through, and the new sanitizer fails with `json-lines sanitizer rejected <batch>`, so the run log batch is lost or the skill stalls. Add explicit `jq -c -Rs` composition instructions or a small shared composer for both batches, then test the happy path through `log-phase.sh` / the Step 9a.1 OOS append path.\n- **Reviewer**: codex-generalist-output.txt\n- **Concern**: 1. **Important** `risk-integration` `scripts/larch-log-batches.sh:12`, `scripts/larch-log-batches.sh:17`: the branch makes `review-findings` and `oos-issues` reject non-JSON append payloads, but the prompt call sites still do not define a concrete NDJSON record composer. `skills/review/SKILL.md:55` only tells the orchestrator to write `review-findings`, and `skills/implement/SKILL.md:44` / `skills/implement/SKILL.md:1740` still describe the OOS append flow without showing how to wrap the markdown blocks into one JSON line. Concrete failure path: a `/review` or `/implement` run reaches those append steps with the existing markdown findings/OOS artifact, `log-phase.sh` or `larch-log.sh append` passes it through, and the new sanitizer fails with `json-lines sanitizer rejected <batch>`, so the run log batch is lost or the skill stalls. Add explicit `jq -c -Rs` composition instructions or a small shared composer for both batches, then test the happy path through `log-phase.sh` / the Step 9a.1 OOS append path.\n- **Suggested revision**: Address the concern above.\n\n### FINDING_6: **Important** `risk-integration` — [`larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/manifest.json`](larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/manifest.json):1-20 (and sibling [`plan-goals-test.md`](larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/plan-goals-test.md), [`plan-review-tally.json`](larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/plan-review-tally.json)): The branch adds a full implement run directory that is not part of the feature description (sanitizer + scripts + tests + docs only). **Completeness w.r.t. plan** / **requirements**: neither the plan nor the feature asked to commit new `larch-logs/...` artifacts. **Concrete scenario**: Merging ships unrelated churn; `manifest.json` records `operator_cwd` / `operator_repo_root` as absolute paths and `status: \"in-progress\"`, which is noise for consumers and slightly widens accidental disclosure of machine layout. **Suggested fix**: Remove these paths from the PR (or split into a separate, explicitly justified run-log commit per repo policy); keep the functional diff limited to `scripts/` as scoped.\n- **Reviewer**: cursor-specialist-correctness-output.txt\n- **Concern**: 1. **Important** `risk-integration` — [`larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/manifest.json`](larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/manifest.json):1-20 (and sibling [`plan-goals-test.md`](larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/plan-goals-test.md), [`plan-review-tally.json`](larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/plan-review-tally.json)): The branch adds a full implement run directory that is not part of the feature description (sanitizer + scripts + tests + docs only). **Completeness w.r.t. plan** / **requirements**: neither the plan nor the feature asked to commit new `larch-logs/...` artifacts. **Concrete scenario**: Merging ships unrelated churn; `manifest.json` records `operator_cwd` / `operator_repo_root` as absolute paths and `status: \"in-progress\"`, which is noise for consumers and slightly widens accidental disclosure of machine layout. **Suggested fix**: Remove these paths from the PR (or split into a separate, explicitly justified run-log commit per repo policy); keep the functional diff limited to `scripts/` as scoped.\n- **Suggested revision**: Address the concern above.\n\n### FINDING_7: **Latent** `risk-integration` — Feature text asks to audit [`scripts/append-execution-issue.sh`](scripts/append-execution-issue.sh) and [`scripts/append-tool-failure.sh`](scripts/append-tool-failure.sh) for “valid JSON”; the diff does not add comments or tests tying them to NDJSON. **Plan-correctness / requirements**: Those scripts append **markdown** into a caller-chosen `LOG_FILE` via awk ([`append-execution-issue.sh`](scripts/append-execution-issue.sh):118-156); [`append-tool-failure.sh`](scripts/append-tool-failure.sh):131-148 builds markdown and calls `append-execution-issue.sh`. They do **not** call `larch-log.sh append` on `execution-issues.ndjson`. **Concrete scenario**: A follow-up “fix” mistakenly rewrites them to emit raw NDJSON into the markdown log. **Suggested fix**: In the PR description, one line stating NDJSON append is only via `larch-log.sh` / orchestrator / [`scripts/implement-finalize.sh`](scripts/implement-finalize.sh) (jq/python path ~256-357) so the audit is closed without code churn.\n- **Reviewer**: cursor-specialist-correctness-output.txt\n- **Concern**: 2. **Latent** `risk-integration` — Feature text asks to audit [`scripts/append-execution-issue.sh`](scripts/append-execution-issue.sh) and [`scripts/append-tool-failure.sh`](scripts/append-tool-failure.sh) for “valid JSON”; the diff does not add comments or tests tying them to NDJSON. **Plan-correctness / requirements**: Those scripts append **markdown** into a caller-chosen `LOG_FILE` via awk ([`append-execution-issue.sh`](scripts/append-execution-issue.sh):118-156); [`append-tool-failure.sh`](scripts/append-tool-failure.sh):131-148 builds markdown and calls `append-execution-issue.sh`. They do **not** call `larch-log.sh append` on `execution-issues.ndjson`. **Concrete scenario**: A follow-up “fix” mistakenly rewrites them to emit raw NDJSON into the markdown log. **Suggested fix**: In the PR description, one line stating NDJSON append is only via `larch-log.sh` / orchestrator / [`scripts/implement-finalize.sh`](scripts/implement-finalize.sh) (jq/python path ~256-357) so the audit is closed without code churn.\n- **Suggested revision**: Address the concern above.\n\n### FINDING_8: **Nit** `code-quality` (plan) — [`scripts/test-larch-log.sh:95-100`](scripts/test-larch-log.sh): After three rejection attempts, only `execution-issues.ndjson` line count is checked because earlier tests only append valid JSON there; `review-findings` and `oos-issues` never receive a successful append first, so the harness does not prove those files stayed absent or unchanged if a buggy path wrote partial data. **Suggested fix:** Optionally seed one valid NDJSON line per batch before the markdown rejects, then assert all three files’ line counts stay at 1 (or add a lower-level unit test on the sanitizer path only).\n- **Reviewer**: cursor-specialist-structure-output.txt\n- **Concern**: 2. **Nit** `code-quality` (plan) — [`scripts/test-larch-log.sh:95-100`](scripts/test-larch-log.sh): After three rejection attempts, only `execution-issues.ndjson` line count is checked because earlier tests only append valid JSON there; `review-findings` and `oos-issues` never receive a successful append first, so the harness does not prove those files stayed absent or unchanged if a buggy path wrote partial data. **Suggested fix:** Optionally seed one valid NDJSON line per batch before the markdown rejects, then assert all three files’ line counts stay at 1 (or add a lower-level unit test on the sanitizer path only).\n- **Suggested revision**: Address the concern above.\n\n### FINDING_9: **Nit** `code-quality` — [`scripts/larch-log-batches.md:21-25`](scripts/larch-log-batches.md): The phrase “composer input” is a bit narrow for `execution-issues` / `review-findings`, which are often produced by `jq` or other orchestrator steps, not only a dedicated composer script. **Suggested fix:** Rephrase to “caller-supplied structured payload (for example composed with `jq`)” or similar.\n- **Reviewer**: cursor-specialist-structure-output.txt\n- **Concern**: 3. **Nit** `code-quality` — [`scripts/larch-log-batches.md:21-25`](scripts/larch-log-batches.md): The phrase “composer input” is a bit narrow for `execution-issues` / `review-findings`, which are often produced by `jq` or other orchestrator steps, not only a dedicated composer script. **Suggested fix:** Rephrase to “caller-supplied structured payload (for example composed with `jq`)” or similar.\n- **Suggested revision**: Address the concern above.\n\n### FINDING_10: **Nit**, `risk-integration`, `scripts/test-larch-log.sh:95-100`: After three `assert_append_rejects_markdown` calls, the harness only re-checks `execution-issues.ndjson` line count stays `2`. **Concrete scenario:** A hypothetical regression that only broke append rejection for `review-findings` or `oos-issues` while still rejecting `execution-issues` would not be caught by this assertion alone (shared code path makes it unlikely). **Suggested fix:** Optionally assert `review-findings.ndjson` / `oos-issues.ndjson` are still absent or unchanged when expected.\n- **Reviewer**: cursor-specialist-edge-cases-output.txt\n- **Concern**: 2. **Nit**, `risk-integration`, `scripts/test-larch-log.sh:95-100`: After three `assert_append_rejects_markdown` calls, the harness only re-checks `execution-issues.ndjson` line count stays `2`. **Concrete scenario:** A hypothetical regression that only broke append rejection for `review-findings` or `oos-issues` while still rejecting `execution-issues` would not be caught by this assertion alone (shared code path makes it unlikely). **Suggested fix:** Optionally assert `review-findings.ndjson` / `oos-issues.ndjson` are still absent or unchanged when expected.\n- **Suggested revision**: Address the concern above.\n\n### FINDING_11: **Plan / requirements check:** The diff matches the plan for [`scripts/larch-log-batches.sh`](scripts/larch-log-batches.sh), [`scripts/larch-log-batches.md`](scripts/larch-log-batches.md), [`scripts/test-larch-log.sh`](scripts/test-larch-log.sh), and [`scripts/test-larch-log.md`](scripts/test-larch-log.md). Call-site script edits were not required by the written plan (audit-only). CI runs `make test-harnesses-4`, which includes `test-larch-log` ([`Makefile:32`](Makefile) and [`Makefile:465-466`](Makefile)), so the new cases are on the critical path once the blocking committed `larch-logs/` noise is removed.\n- **Reviewer**: \n- **Concern**: \n- **Suggested revision**: Address the concern above.\n\n### FINDING_12: **Plan alignment (structure):** Table updates in [`scripts/larch-log-batches.sh`](scripts/larch-log-batches.sh), documentation in [`scripts/larch-log-batches.md`](scripts/larch-log-batches.md), harness and contract doc in [`scripts/test-larch-log.sh`](scripts/test-larch-log.sh) / [`scripts/test-larch-log.md`](scripts/test-larch-log.md) match the plan; the substring asserted in tests matches the prefix of [`scripts/lib-larch-log.sh:150-151`](scripts/lib-larch-log.sh) (`json-lines sanitizer rejected $batch: invalid JSON line`). No `CreatePlan` artifact was produced because this turn is a review-only deliverable, not an implementation plan.\n- **Reviewer**: \n- **Concern**: \n- **Suggested revision**: Address the concern above.\n\n### FINDING_13: **Plan fidelity walk (summary):**\n- **Reviewer**: \n- **Concern**: \n- **Suggested revision**: Address the concern above.\n\n### FINDING_14: **Read-only note:** Hard constraints forbid writing files, so the TSV sid