./larch-logs/implement/F17AB4A1-6889-4B78-8965-EE6C703494CC/review-findings-full.jsonl:4:{"id":"FINDING_5","issue_number":"0","phase":"code-review","outcome":"accepted","schema_version":"2","reviewer_slots":["cursor-specialist-structure-output.txt","cursor-specialist-correctness-output.txt","cursor-specialist-testing-output.txt","cursor-specialist-edge-cases-output.txt","cursor-specialist-plan-fidelity-output.txt"],"round_num":"1","category":"Automated tests omit the planned probe-failure / exit-2 regression case","prose_body":"## Automated tests omit the planned probe-failure / exit-2 regression case\n\n- **Reviewer(s)**: cursor-specialist-structure-output.txt, cursor-specialist-correctness-output.txt, cursor-specialist-testing-output.txt, cursor-specialist-edge-cases-output.txt, cursor-specialist-plan-fidelity-output.txt\n- **Concern**: The implementation plan calls for a probe-failure scenario (`SYNC_STATUS=probe-error`, exit `2`), but `scripts/test-check-main-sync.sh` / related docs do not exercise it, so regressions in probe handling, `rev-list` edge cases, and caller mapping for exit `2` can ship without CI signal.\n- **Suggested revision**: Add a controlled fixture (for example git wrapper, invalid `GIT_DIR`, or sterile repo) asserting stdout/`SYNC_STATUS` and exit code `2`, and align `scripts/test-check-main-sync.md` with the harness."}
