./larch-logs/implement/EF527D59-EE0F-4DCC-B3E0-57277F4006D3/round-3/review-round-summary.md:25:- **Concern**: [important] Implementation plan specified replacing sort -u with cp so duplicate identical TSV rows still reach the LLM aggregator; branch uses awk '!seen[$0]++' which still drops identical full rows before aggregation. Two overlapping collector paths could emit the same title/label/body line twice; with awk they collapse to one pre-aggregator row, so the aggregator never sees the duplicate attribution the plan assumed would still exist. Use cp as planned if aggregator-owned dedup is desired, or keep awk and update plan/docs with explicit rationale for row-level dedup vs aggregator dedup.
./larch-logs/implement/AD2E81EA-F212-47D8-B5C0-9F7AC6413215/plan-goals-test.md:7:Lower the "coder simplicity override" threshold in `skills/implement/SKILL.md` from `diff_lines < 30` (bypass external coder for changes under 30 lines) to `diff_lines <= 3` (bypass external coder only for truly trivial ≤3-line changes). This ensures the main agent only self-implements when the planned change is ≤3 lines; all larger changes are delegated to an external coder.
./larch-logs/implement/5F7568AE-E8DA-4B76-8E08-E03C1DA604FC/round-2/findings.md:51:### FINDING_11: **`risk-integration` (plan / requirements)** — **Important** — [`skills/implement/SKILL.md`](skills/implement/SKILL.md) (Step 7a prose, ~lines where the pre-bump flush is documented): The umbrella `<feature_description>` and plan Part B require calling `write-final-report.sh` **before** merge (between Step 7a and Step 8) so `final-summary.md` is included in the pre-bump `larch-log` commit and is not suppressed by the post-merge sentinel. The branch instead **explicitly forbids** calling `write-final-report.sh` in Step 7a and points operators to Step 17/18 ([`skills/implement/scripts/write-final-report.md`](skills/implement/scripts/write-final-report.md) updated the same way). **Concrete scenario:** A successful merge still follows the old timing: `write-final-report` after `ship-pr.sh` creates `post-merge-sentinel`, so `larch-log.sh commit` can still refuse to pick up `final-summary.md` for the PR-embedded run-log—exactly the regression Part B was meant to fix. **Suggested fix:** Either implement the planned pre-bump call (accepting `PR: N/A` in that snapshot) or amend the issue/feature text and add an alternate fix (e.g. teach `larch-log.sh` / `refresh-run-logs.sh` to commit `final-summary` before the sentinel) and add a regression test that reproduces the sentinel interaction.
./larch-logs/implement/5F7568AE-E8DA-4B76-8E08-E03C1DA604FC/round-2/findings.md:53:- **Concern**: 1. **`risk-integration` (plan / requirements)** — **Important** — [`skills/implement/SKILL.md`](skills/implement/SKILL.md) (Step 7a prose, ~lines where the pre-bump flush is documented): The umbrella `<feature_description>` and plan Part B require calling `write-final-report.sh` **before** merge (between Step 7a and Step 8) so `final-summary.md` is included in the pre-bump `larch-log` commit and is not suppressed by the post-merge sentinel. The branch instead **explicitly forbids** calling `write-final-report.sh` in Step 7a and points operators to Step 17/18 ([`skills/implement/scripts/write-final-report.md`](skills/implement/scripts/write-final-report.md) updated the same way). **Concrete scenario:** A successful merge still follows the old timing: `write-final-report` after `ship-pr.sh` creates `post-merge-sentinel`, so `larch-log.sh commit` can still refuse to pick up `final-summary.md` for the PR-embedded run-log—exactly the regression Part B was meant to fix. **Suggested fix:** Either implement the planned pre-bump call (accepting `PR: N/A` in that snapshot) or amend the issue/feature text and add an alternate fix (e.g. teach `larch-log.sh` / `refresh-run-logs.sh` to commit `final-summary` before the sentinel) and add a regression test that reproduces the sentinel interaction.
./larch-logs/implement/5F7568AE-E8DA-4B76-8E08-E03C1DA604FC/round-2/findings.md:93:- **Concern**: [important] Part B (pre-merge write-final-report before larch-log commit) not implemented; Step 7a text forbids write-final-report until ship-pr-state exists. Feature/plan require write-final-report before merge sentinel so final-summary can be committed pre-sentinel; branch defers to Step 17/18, so successful-merge runs can still miss committed final-summary when post-merge sentinel blocks larch-log commit. Implement planned Step 7a write-final-report (with documented provisional PR_URL / missing merge SHA) or add another commit path before sentinel; align SKILL.md with agreed spec.
./larch-logs/implement/5F7568AE-E8DA-4B76-8E08-E03C1DA604FC/round-2/findings.md:98:- **Concern**: [important] Part B of the plan is not implemented; Step 7a explicitly avoids write-final-report and defers to Step 17/18. Successful merges still hit post-merge-sentinel before terminal final-summary writes, so larch-log commits for final-summary can remain suppressed—the original regression the plan aimed to fix persists. Implement the planned pre-bump write-final-report (before larch-log commit) or adjust sentinel/larch-log rules and update the plan accordingly.
./larch-logs/implement/5F7568AE-E8DA-4B76-8E08-E03C1DA604FC/round-2/findings.md:108:- **Concern**: [important] Step 7a forbids write-final-report.sh before Step 8+ instead of the planned pre-larch-log commit call. Post-merge sentinel can still suppress committing final-summary.md in the pre-bump PR window for successful merges. Add pre-sentinel write-final-report (or equivalent) so final-summary is committed before post-merge-sentinel; drop the prohibition if that path is adopted.
