./larch-logs/implement/C5B28F06-C105-4ECC-B99A-59C3023BFB0E/execution-issues.ndjson:2:{"phase":"implement","step":"7a","category":"In-Scope Findings","source":"execution-issues.md pre-bump","source_sha256":"911e07a7f90cf3a0d8dc9dbc2a65cf927bcdb8ce4795edcb44f959d34cfcbaf4","body":"\n1. **Important** `correctness` [Implementation plan §“Edge Cases” / `prefix_records` behavior] — The plan states the `user:attachment` branch must **not** set `included_initial` so a plain-text initial user (when it appears **before** attachment in the parent chain) can still be captured as `user:initial`. The implementation sets `included_initial = True` inside the `user:attachment` branch at [scripts/cache-key-runtime-audit.py:332-335](scripts/cache-key-runtime-audit.py). Concrete impact: any later plain `user` bubble in the same prefix walk no longer qualifies for `user:initial` once an attachment user has been seen, which diverges from the plan’s explicit `included_initial` story (even though it matches [scripts/test-cache-key-runtime-audit.sh:135-146](scripts/test-cache-key-runtime-audit.sh) `write_attachment_then_text_fixture`). Suggested fix: either remove the `included_initial` assignment from the attachment branch and adjust tests/docs, or revise the plan/contract bullet so it matches the shipped semantics.\n\n2. **Important** `risk-integration` [Implementation plan §“Files to Modify”] — The plan lists only four paths (`scripts/cache-key-runtime-audit.py`, `scripts/test-cache-key-runtime-audit.sh`, `scripts/cache-key-runtime-audit.md`, `scripts/test-cache-key-runtime-audit.md`). The branch also adds committed implement run artifacts under [larch-logs/implement/C5B28F06-C105-4ECC-B99A-59C3023BFB0E/](larch-logs/implement/C5B28F06-C105-4ECC-B99A-59C3023BFB0E/) (e.g. [larch-logs/implement/C5B28F06-C105-4ECC-B99A-59C3023BFB0E/manifest.json](larch-logs/implement/C5B28F06-C105-4ECC-B99A-59C3023BFB0E/manifest.json), [larch-logs/implement/C5B28F06-C105-4ECC-B99A-59C3023BFB0E/code-review-tally.json](larch-logs/implement/C5B28F06-C105-4ECC-B99A-59C3023BFB0E/code-review-tally.json), [larch-logs/implement/C5B28F06-C105-4ECC-B99A-59C3023BFB0E/review-findings-full.md](larch-logs/implement/C5B28F06-C105-4ECC-B99A-59C3023BFB0E/review-findings-full.md), [larch-logs/implement/C5B28F06-C105-4ECC-B99A-59C3023BFB0E/plan-goals-test.md](larch-logs/implement/C5B28F06-C105-4ECC-B99A-59C3023BFB0E/plan-goals-test.md)). That is out-of-band versus the stated file list and couples the feature to a specific run id. Suggested fix: drop these from the feature branch unless a documented run-log policy explicitly requires them, or extend the plan/PR scope to justify them.\n\n3. **Nit** `correctness` [Implementation plan §1 `content_to_text()`] — The plan prescribes `json.dumps(item, …)` for `tool_result` / `tool_use` blocks to preserve all fields. The implementation instead routes non-`text` dict/list blocks through `summarize_attachment_block()` ([scripts/cache-key-runtime-audit.py:334-367](scripts/cache-key-runtime-audit.py)), emitting `type` plus `payload_sha256` only in rendered/digested prefix material. This is consistent with the updated contract in [scripts/cache-key-runtime-audit.md](scripts/cache-key-runtime-audit.md) and [SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md), but it is a literal deviation from the pasted implementation plan text and from the plan’s stated side effect about `\"tool_use_id\"` appearing in flattened `entry_content`. Suggested fix: amend the authoritative plan/spec to describe redacted summaries (or revert to full JSON if that remains the source of truth).\n\n**Plan completeness (positive, no severity):** `_is_attachment_bearing` dict-shaped `message.content` handling ([scripts/cache-key-runtime-audit.py:304-305](scripts/cache-key-runtime-audit.py)), extra harness scenarios (`write_attachment_dict_fixture`, `write_tool_use_mutation_fixture`, `write_attachment_then_text_fixture`), and branched `parentUuid: sys1` mutation shapes ([scripts/test-cache-key-runtime-audit.sh:75-132](scripts/test-cache-key-runtime-audit.sh)) satisfy or exceed the plan’s functional intent (attachment-bearing users in the stable prefix, `CACHE-INVALIDATING` on same-slot drift, redacted reports).\n\n**Commits on branch since merge-base with `main`:** `3e57ba64` Fix stable-prefix audit…; `d525a4bc` / `f02d77e1` chore(larch-logs)…; `57e52ef5` / `d6546c31` Address code review feedback.\n\n---\n\nRead-only mode: TSV sidecar file was not written. Records below use tabs; replace literal newlines in fields with space if you ingest them.\n\n```tsv\nschema_version\tscope\tseverity\tfocus_area\tlocation\twhat\tscenario_or_breakage\tsuggested_fix\n1\tin_scope\timportant\tcorrectness\tscripts/cache-key-runtime-audit.py:332-335\tuser:attachment sets included_initial=True, contradicting plan Edge Cases bullet\tPlan promised attachment path does not flip included_initial so earlier/later plain user:initial eligibility matches that story; shipped code suppresses later plain user:initial after an attachment user in the same chain walk\tRemove included_initial mutation from attachment branch and retest, or update plan/contract to the new semantics\n1\tin_scope\timportant\trisk-integration\tlarch-logs/implement/C5B28F06-C105-4ECC-B99A-59C3023BFB0E/ (manifest.json, code-review-tally.json, review-findings-full.md, plan-goals-test.md, plan-review-tally.json)\tCommitted implement run artifacts not listed under plan Files to Modify\tFeature PR scope exceeds the four planned paths and pins private review metadata into version control\tRemove larch-logs changes from the feature branch or expand the plan/PR scope with an explicit run-log justification\n1\tin_scope\tnit\tcorrectness\tscripts/cache-key-runtime-audit.py:281-367\tcontent_to_text uses summarized attachment blocks, not full JSON.dumps for tool_result/tool_use per plan §1\tLiteral plan-to-code mismatch on serialization shape; docs/SECURITY describe redaction instead\tReconcile the written implementation plan with scripts/cache-key-runtime-audit.md or restore full JSON if that remains authoritative\n```\n  ```\n"}
./larch-logs/implement/C5B28F06-C105-4ECC-B99A-59C3023BFB0E/execution-issues.ndjson:23:{"phase":"implement","step":"7a","category":"Out-of-Scope Observations","source":"execution-issues.md pre-bump","source_sha256":"b9994d61fa04d1b989d2bf6cb5e2f0cb53a5850acd2909634d32dedd997b5b0d","body":"\nNone worth listing; no pre-existing defects were re-scanned beyond plan traceability.\n\n---\n\n**Read-only constraint:** Per your instructions, no `.tsv` sidecar file was written. Below is the TSV payload you can save manually if needed.\n\n```text\nschema_version\tscope\tseverity\tfocus_area\tlocation\twhat\tscenario_or_breakage\tsuggested_fix\n1\tin_scope\timportant\tcorrectness\tscripts/test-cache-key-runtime-audit.sh:99-195\twrite_attachment_stable_fixture omits planned second identical tool_result turn\tPlan §4 requires two turns with same tool_result content for EXPECTED-GROWTH; fixture uses plain-text usr2 so coverage and pass message imply a scenario the plan did not describe\tUse two tool_result user turns with identical JSON per plan, or revise plan and comments to match the implemented user:initial extension case\n1\tin_scope\tnit\trisk-integration\tlarch-logs/implement/C5B28F06-C105-4ECC-B99A-59C3023BFB0E/\tImplement run log files added though not in plan file list\tPR scope exceeds the four paths listed under Files to Modify\tKeep logs out of the feature commit or justify in plan/PR\n1\tin_scope\tnit\tcorrectness\tscripts/test-cache-key-runtime-audit.sh:191-194\tHarness pass message over-claims tool_result stability across turns\tMessage suggests both turns exercise identical tool_result prefix; second turn is plain text\tRename pass message/fixture description to match actual prefix composition\n```\n  ```\n"}
