/bin/bash -lc "nl -ba scripts/larch-log.md | sed -n '1,80p'" in <OPERATOR_REPO_PATH>
 succeeded in 0ms:
     1	# larch-log.sh contract
     2	
     3	`scripts/larch-log.sh` is the router for committed larch runtime logs under
     4	`larch-logs/<skill>/<run-id>/`.
     5	
     6	Primary verbs:
     7	
     8	- `init` creates `manifest.json`. Schema version 2 records redacted provenance
     9	  placeholders: `operator_cwd` is the stable string `"<OPERATOR_CWD>"`,
    10	  `operator_repo_root` is `"<REPO_ROOT>"` when the caller is inside a git repo
    11	  and `null` otherwise, and `model_roster.main` comes from
    12	  `${CLAUDE_CODE_MODEL:-${CLAUDE_MODEL:-unknown}}`. The manifest keeps these
    13	  fields for schema compatibility without committing operator-local absolute
    14	  paths. New runs include an empty `steps_ran` object for per-step skip flags;
    15	  `pr_number` and in-progress `status` are not written at init (post-flush
    16	  lifecycle fields are owned by explicit flush paths and recovery tagging).
    17	- `write` atomically replaces replace-mode batches.
    18	- `write-round` copies registered per-round review artifacts from
    19	  `--source-dir` into `round-<N>/` under the run directory. It strips `CMD_JSON`
    20	  lines from `.meta` sidecars and removes top-level `.result` from included
    21	  `*-output.txt.json` / `*-output-*.txt.json` tool-envelope sidecars before
    22	  applying the normal tmpdir and secrets redaction. Session tmpdirs may retain
    23	  raw `.meta` / JSON sidecars for retry state, but committed `round-<N>/`
    24	  artifacts always use the trimmed form and fail closed if trimming fails. It
    25	  writes only to the log root; `commit` later picks up the round directory.
    26	  The allow-list includes scout artifacts (`scout-round*-status.env`,
    27	  `scout-round*-manifest.json`, `scout-round*-manifest.json.raw`), dynamic-archetype files
    28	  (`reviewer-dyn-*.md`, `dyn-*-prompt.md`), voter parse-retry first-pass sidecars
    29	  (`*-vote-output-first-pass.txt`), and NS-retry specialist first-pass sidecars
    30	  (`*-output-first-pass.txt`). Files under `dynamic-archetypes/`
    31	  inside `--source-dir` are walked one level deep and flattened to the round
    32	  root (no nested `dynamic-archetypes/` directory in committed output).
    33	- `append` atomically appends append-mode NDJSON batches.
    34	- `exists` probes a batch path.
    35	- `manifest` updates mutable manifest fields. Dotted keys `steps_ran.<step>` set per-step boolean flags under `.steps_ran` (shell step name after the dot; value must be `true` or `false`). Other keys use flat `field=value` syntax. Values that look like JSON-native scalars (`null`, `true`, `false`, integers) are passed via `--argjson` so they are stored with the correct JSON type; all other values are passed via `--arg` (stored as strings).
    36	- `commit` stages and commits one run directory without pushing. It refuses
    37	  with a stderr diagnostic when `$IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR/post-merge-sentinel` exists
    38	  or when the current branch is `main`/the `origin/HEAD` default branch,
    39	  preventing incidental post-merge log-only commits from prompt-side and
    40	  refresh paths. This rejection is unconditional — no bypass env var is
    41	  honored (see `skills/implement/SKILL.md` NEVER #19).
    42	
    43	Every verb emits a quiet KEY=value envelope:
    44	
    45	```text
    46	LOG_WRITTEN=true|false
    47	LOG_PATH=<path>
    48	BYTES=<n>
    49	SHA256=<hex>
    50	COMMIT_SHA=<sha-or-empty>
    51	UNCHANGED=true|false
    52	```
    53	
    54	Payload content is never written to stdout. Payloads pass through
    55	`redact-tmpdir-paths.sh` and `redact-secrets.sh`. `write-round` applies
    56	sidecar-specific trimmers from `scripts/lib-redact.sh` before this shared
    57	redaction pipeline. Batches that declare the
    58	`plan-goals` sanitizer must contain a non-empty `## Implementation Plan` section
    59	that is not a pointer-only placeholder. Batches that declare the `json-lines`
    60	sanitizer must be empty or contain one valid JSON value per non-empty line.
    61	Batches that declare the `json-object` sanitizer must parse as one JSON object.
    62	Batches that declare the `mermaid` sanitizer (in `larch-log-batches.sh`) also use
    63	`sanitize-mermaid-fragment.sh --from-md` and fail closed on rejection; no
    64	current batch uses the Mermaid sanitizer — it is reserved for future opt-in.
    65	
    66	**Log-root resolution** is single-tier (see `lib-larch-log.sh`):
    67	
    68	1. `$LARCH_LOG_ROOT`, set by the required `--log-root <dir>` flag or explicitly
    69	   exported for test isolation.
    70	
    71	The `init`, `write`, `write-round`, `append`, `exists`, `manifest`, and `commit` verbs require
    72	an absolute `--log-root <dir>` unless `$LARCH_LOG_ROOT` is already exported.
    73	`/implement` passes `$IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR/larch-logs` explicitly so in-progress
    74	runtime payloads stay out of the git working tree until `commit` is called.
    75	
    76	`REPO_ROOT` (used by `commit`) and `LARCH_LOG_REPO_ROOT` (used by `commit` via
    77	`larch_log_repo_run_dir`) both resolve via `git -C "$PWD" rev-parse --show-toplevel`
    78	at script load time so logs land in the consumer repo rather than the plugin install
    79	cache. Both remain empty when invoked outside a git worktree; `commit` fails with
    80	a descriptive error in that case.

